{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Combinatorics.Young.SemistandardTableau","lean:module:Mathlib.SetTheory.Cardinal.Finite","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RSKBurnsideTarget","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneC8SuperExpBound","lean:module:QOU.Mass.SumSYTEqInvolution"],"declarations":49,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.c8_superexp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.c8_superexp","kind":"theorem","line":632,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L632-L677","doc":"**C8 super-exponential lower bound (`§3b`-conditional on `[RSKIdentitiesContext]`).**\nThis said \"unconditional modulo the two remaining RSK `sorry`s above\"; there are no\n`sorry`s above — the two RSK identities are fields of the `[RSKIdentitiesContext]`\nhypothesis this theorem also takes, so the conditionality is in the signature and\n`#print axioms` here is clean. Instantiating the sibling arithmetic core `c8_lower_bound`\nwith `f = f^λ = dimSYT`, `g = f^{λ/(2,1)}`, `kfac = k!`, `Ik = I(k)`, and\ndischarging its inputs by casting `branching_two_one` (A) and `skew_le_straight` +\n`sum_dimSYT_eq_involution` (C) to `ℝ`, the Plancherel-weighted branched sum obeys\n\n    k! / (9·I(k))  ≤  (Σ_{λ⊢k} (f^λ)² f^{λ/(2,1)}) / k!.\n\nAll positivity and arithmetic are proved here. (A) and (C) are *hypotheses* of this\nstatement, not RSK inputs: (C) is proved outright above, and (A) is `branching_two_one`,\nwhose class is discharged in `QOU.Mathlib.SkewBranchingTwoOne`. So this bound now holds at\nevery concrete `k ≥ 3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.sum_dimSYT_eq_involution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.sum_dimSYT_eq_involution","kind":"theorem","line":611,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L611-L628","doc":"**RSK for involutions.** `Σ_{λ⊢k} f^λ = I(k)`, the number of involutions in `S_k` — the\n`q = 1` value of the QOU na-Stokes period.  **Unconditional**, and it needs no instance.\n\nUntil 2026-08-30 this was a field of `RSKIdentitiesContext` and this docstring said the\nidentity \"requires massive infrastructure (the RSK correspondence)\" and was \"an open gap\".\n**That was a mis-diagnosis, not merely a stale status note**: the identity does not need RSK\nat all.  Young's lattice is a `1`-differential poset, and that route proves it with finite\ncombinatorics on `YoungDiagram` — no insertion, no bumping, no permutation↔tableau-pair\nbijection.  See `QOU.Mass.sum_dimSYT_eq_involution_keystone`, and `QOU.Mathlib.upSum_eq` for\nthe up-operator step the whole argument turns on.\n\nThe lesson is worth keeping: *\"Mathlib lacks X, therefore blocked\"* is sound only when `X` is\nactually required.  Here the standard textbook route was mistaken for the only route, and that\nmistake was recorded in this file, in two beans and in three other docstrings as though it\nwere an infrastructure fact. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.skew_le_straight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.skew_le_straight","kind":"theorem","line":587,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L587-L609","doc":"**Skew SYT inject into straight SYT (PROVED, no longer cited).**\n`Σ_{λ⊢k} f^{λ/(2,1)} ≤ Σ_{λ⊢k} f^λ`, the latter being the involution number\n`I(k)` (RSK for involutions, below).\n\nProved term by term, by the explicit extension `straightOfSkew`: fill `(2,1)`\nwith `κ = 1,2,3` and shift each skew value into `{4, …, |λ|}`.  Shapes not\ncontaining `(2,1)` contribute `0` on the left by the `fDimSkew` guard, so nothing\nis needed for them.  No Jacobi–Trudi and no RSK: the *inequality* is elementary\nonce the injection is written down.\n\n(This used to close by saying \"only the two *equalities* — `branching_two_one`,\n`sum_dimSYT_eq_involution` — need the real machinery\". Both are now proved, and **neither**\nneeded it. What is true is the weaker claim that an inequality needs only an injection while\nan equality needs a bijection.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.branching_two_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.branching_two_one","kind":"theorem","line":552,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L552-L585","doc":"**Classical branching** `Σ_{λ⊢k} f^λ · f^{λ/(2,1)} = k! · f^{(2,1)} / |(2,1)|!`\nat `μ = (2,1)` (where `f^{(2,1)} = 2`, `|(2,1)|! = 6`, so the RHS is `k!/3`).\nStated in the cast-clean form `3 · (Σ …) = k!`, valid for `k ≥ |μ| = 3`.\n\nRepresentation-theoretically this is the dimension of\n`Ind_{S_m × S_{k−m}}^{S_k}(S^μ ⊠ ℚ[S_{k−m}])` counted two ways: `k!·f^μ/m!` by the\nindex-times-dimension formula, and `Σ_λ f^{λ/μ} f^λ` by `s_μ·s_1^{k−m} =\nΣ_λ f^{λ/μ} s_λ`.\n\n**Only true because `fDimSkew` guards on containment** — the sum must skip every\n`λ` not containing `(2,1)`.  See `skewSYT_nonempty_of_not_le`, which exhibits the\ncounterexample the guard removes and checks this identity at `k = 3, 4`.\n\nThe body is `ctx.branching_two_one`, the matching field of the `[RSKIdentitiesContext]`\nhypothesis, so the hypothesis sits in the signature rather than in the term and\n`#print axioms` on this declaration is clean.\n\n**No longer a gap (2026-08-31).** `QOU.Mathlib.SkewBranchingTwoOne.branching_two_one_holds`\nproves this statement unconditionally and registers `rskIdentitiesContextInstance`, so the\n`[ctx]` here resolves and the theorem applies at every concrete `k ≥ 3`. It is kept in\nconditional form only because `SkewStandardYoungTableau` and `fDimSkew` are defined in *this*\nfile, so the proof has to live downstream of it.\n\n**And it did not need RSK.** This docstring used to say the identity \"requires massive\ninfrastructure (the RSK correspondence and hook-length formula)\". The proof uses neither: it\nis `|μ|!·∑_λ f^λ f^{λ/μ} = k!·f^μ` (`QOU.Mathlib.factorial_mul_skewPair_of_le`) at\n`μ = (2,1)`, which is the skew branching rule plus the up-operator identity — finite\ncombinatorics on `YoungDiagram`. The one shelf item is the single number `f^{(2,1)} = 2`,\nfrom the `decide`-verified small-`n` hook bridge: a computation on one three-cell shape, not\nthe hook-length formula as a theorem. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.RSKIdentitiesContext.branching_two_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.RSKIdentitiesContext.branching_two_one","kind":"theorem","line":550,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L550-L550","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.RSKIdentitiesContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.RSKIdentitiesContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":549,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L549-L549","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.RSKIdentitiesContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.RSKIdentitiesContext","kind":"class","line":549,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L549-L550","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.involutionNumber_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.involutionNumber_pos","kind":"theorem","line":476,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L476-L487","doc":"The involution numbers are strictly positive (`I(n) ≥ 1`). Needed as the C8\ndenominator `I(k)` must be positive for `k!/(9·I(k))` to be a finite lower\nbound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.card_skew_le_card_straight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.card_skew_le_card_straight","kind":"theorem","line":466,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L466-L470","doc":"**`f^{Y/(2,1)} ≤ f^Y`** whenever `(2,1) ⊆ Y`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.straightOfSkew_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.straightOfSkew_injective","kind":"theorem","line":451,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L451-L464","doc":"The extension is injective: subtracting the shift on the skew cells recovers\nthe skew tableau, and `zeros` pins it everywhere else. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.straightOfSkew","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.straightOfSkew","kind":"def","line":443,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L443-L449","doc":"**The extension.**  A skew SYT of shape `Y/(2,1)` becomes a straight SYT of\n`Y`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.straightEntry_surjOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.straightEntry_surjOn","kind":"theorem","line":414,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L414-L441","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.straightEntry_injOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.straightEntry_injOn","kind":"theorem","line":390,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L390-L412","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.straightEntry_mapsTo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.straightEntry_mapsTo","kind":"theorem","line":370,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L370-L388","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.straightSsyt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.straightSsyt","kind":"def","line":362,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L362-L368","doc":"The straight tableau's underlying semistandard tableau. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.straightEntry_col","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.straightEntry_col","kind":"theorem","line":343,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L343-L360","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.straightEntry_row","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.straightEntry_row","kind":"theorem","line":324,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L324-L341","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.straightEntry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.straightEntry","kind":"def","line":319,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L319-L322","doc":"The straight filling: `(2,1)` gets `κ ∈ {1,2,3}`, each skew cell gets its skew\nvalue shifted to `{4, …, |Y|}`, everything off `Y` gets `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.skew_entry_injOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.skew_entry_injOn","kind":"theorem","line":314,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L314-L317","doc":"Equal cardinalities of source and image make the skew filling injective. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.skew_entry_surj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.skew_entry_surj","kind":"theorem","line":305,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L305-L312","doc":"…and hit every one of them (the `content` field is an equality, not an\ninclusion). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.skew_entry_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.skew_entry_lt","kind":"theorem","line":296,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L296-L303","doc":"Skew entries land in `{0, …, d−1}` (`d` the number of skew cells). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.three_le_card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.three_le_card","kind":"theorem","line":293,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L293-L294","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.skew_card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.skew_card","kind":"theorem","line":289,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L289-L291","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.mu21_cells_subset","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.mu21_cells_subset","kind":"theorem","line":286,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L286-L287","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.kappa21_surj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.kappa21_surj","kind":"theorem","line":274,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L274-L280","doc":"Every value in `{1,2,3}` is realised by `κ` on a cell of `(2,1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.kappa21_injOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.kappa21_injOn","kind":"theorem","line":267,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L267-L272","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.kappa21_col","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.kappa21_col","kind":"theorem","line":261,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L261-L265","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.kappa21_row","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.kappa21_row","kind":"theorem","line":255,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L255-L259","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.kappa21_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.kappa21_le","kind":"theorem","line":252,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L252-L253","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.kappa21_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.kappa21_pos","kind":"theorem","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L249-L250","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.kappa21","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.kappa21","kind":"def","line":246,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L246-L247","doc":"The canonical standard filling of `(2,1)` by `1, 2, 3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.mem_mu21","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.mem_mu21","kind":"theorem","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L241-L244","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.mu21_card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.mu21_card","kind":"theorem","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L239-L239","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.mu21_cells","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.mu21_cells","kind":"theorem","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L236-L237","doc":"The three cells of `(2,1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.skewSYT_nonempty_of_not_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.skewSYT_nonempty_of_not_le","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L172-L220","doc":"**Why `fDimSkew` must guard on containment** (machine-proved, no `sorry`).\n\n`(2,1) ⊄ (3)`, yet `SkewStandardYoungTableau (3) (2,1)` is inhabited: the skew\nregion `(3).cells \\ (2,1).cells` is the single cell `(0,2)`, both strictness\nfields are vacuous there, and the all-zero filling satisfies `zeros` and\n`content`.  So the *raw* `Nat.card` is `1` where the classical `f^{(3)/(2,1)}`\nis `0`.\n\nUnguarded, `branching_two_one` would be **false already at `k = 3`**: the three\npartitions of `3` contribute `f^{(3)}·1 + f^{(2,1)}·1 + f^{(1,1,1)}·1\n= 1 + 2 + 1 = 4` (each raw skew count is `1`, the shapes `(3)` and `(1,1,1)`\ncontributing spuriously), and `3 · 4 = 12 ≠ 6 = 3!`.  Guarded, only `(2,1)`\nsurvives and the sum is `2`, with `3 · 2 = 6 = 3!` ✓ — and at `k = 4` the\nsurviving shapes `(3,1), (2,2), (2,1,1)` give `3·1 + 2·1 + 3·1 = 8` with\n`3 · 8 = 24 = 4!` ✓. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.row3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.row3","kind":"def","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L167-L170","doc":"The single-row shape `(3)`.  Present only as the witness shape of\n`skewSYT_nonempty_of_not_le`: it is the smallest partition of `3` that does *not*\ncontain `(2,1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.mu21","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.mu21","kind":"def","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L163-L165","doc":"The Young diagram of shape `(2, 1)` — the smallest hook, with `f^{(2,1)} = 2`\nand `|(2,1)|! = 6`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.SkewStandardYoungTableau.ext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.SkewStandardYoungTableau.ext","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L148-L159","doc":"Two skew tableaux with the same entry map are equal (the remaining fields are\npropositions). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.fDimSkew_of_not_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.fDimSkew_of_not_le","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L144-L146","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.fDimSkew_of_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.fDimSkew_of_le","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L140-L142","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.fDimSkew","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.fDimSkew","kind":"def","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L127-L138","doc":"`f^{outer/inner}` — the number of skew standard Young tableaux of shape\n`outer / inner`.\n\n**The containment guard is load-bearing, not defensive.**  The classical skew\ncount is `0` unless `inner ⊆ outer` (the skew shape `λ/μ` is undefined\notherwise), but `SkewStandardYoungTableau` imposes no containment: it fills the\nset difference `outer.cells \\ inner.cells`, which stays perfectly well-behaved —\nand inhabited — when `inner ⊄ outer`.  `skewSYT_nonempty_of_not_le` below exhibits\nthat, and records the arithmetic showing that the unguarded count makes\n`branching_two_one` false. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.SkewStandardYoungTableau.content","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.SkewStandardYoungTableau.content","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L124-L124","doc":"The entries on the skew cells are exactly `{0, …, |diff|−1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.SkewStandardYoungTableau.zeros","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.SkewStandardYoungTableau.zeros","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L122-L122","doc":"`entry` vanishes off the skew region (on `inner`, or outside `outer`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.SkewStandardYoungTableau.col_strict","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.SkewStandardYoungTableau.col_strict","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L119-L119","doc":"Columns are strictly increasing among the skew cells. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.SkewStandardYoungTableau.row_strict","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.SkewStandardYoungTableau.row_strict","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L116-L116","doc":"Rows are strictly increasing among the skew cells. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.SkewStandardYoungTableau.entry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.SkewStandardYoungTableau.entry","kind":"def","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L114-L114","doc":"`entry i j` is the value in cell `(i, j)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.SkewStandardYoungTableau.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.SkewStandardYoungTableau.mk","kind":"ctor","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L112-L112","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.SkewStandardYoungTableau","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.SkewStandardYoungTableau","kind":"structure","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L109-L125","doc":"A **skew standard Young tableau** of shape `outer / inner` is a filling of the\nskew cells `outer.cells \\ inner.cells` by `{0, …, |diff|−1}`, each used once,\nstrictly increasing along rows and columns among the skew (non-`inner`) cells. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.decidableLEYoungDiagram","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.decidableLEYoungDiagram","kind":"instance","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/YoungTableauStandard.lean#L97-L105","doc":"Containment of Young diagrams is decidable — it *is* `Finset` inclusion of the\ncells (`YoungDiagram.cells_subset_iff` is `Iff.rfl`), but instance search cannot\nsee through the `Preorder` instance to find that.  Supplying it keeps `fDimSkew`\nfree of `Classical`, which matters: an ambient classical `DecidableEq (ℕ × ℕ)`\nwould make the `\\` in `Y.cells \\ mu21.cells` elaborate to a different instance\nthan the one in `SkewStandardYoungTableau.content`, and the two would not\nrewrite against each other. ","signatureChunk":0}]}